# Decisions Log

Append-only. Every judgment call made without user input goes here.

Format:
```
[ISO 8601 timestamp] [CONTEXT]
Chose: <option taken>
Over:  <option(s) rejected>
Because: <reasoning>
Reversible: <yes/no — can this be revisited later?>
```

Use this when:
- A function's subsystem assignment is ambiguous (physics or gameplay?)
- A struct field's name is a coin-flip between two valid interpretations
- A base address must be chosen heuristically for an overlay
- The "scope" boundary is unclear (e.g., is this audio-data parsing in-scope or out-of-scope?)
- Any other point where a different reasonable Claude would make a different call

The user reviews this log to spot-check judgment calls.

